    <abstract>
      <para>
       PHP is an open source server-side scripting language designed for Web 
       development. It is used to create dynamic, interactive content that works with databases.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <variablelist>
    <varlistentry>
      <term>Lifecycle category</term>
      <listitem><para>Balanced</para></listitem>
    </varlistentry>
    <varlistentry>
      <term>Versions</term>
      <listitem><para>The starting version is 8.4. A new PHP version is shipped with each &suselinux;&nbsp;16 
          minor release.</para></listitem>
    </varlistentry>
    <varlistentry>
      <term>Release cycle</term>
      <listitem><para>Patch-level updates are delivered throughout the support period of each minor release.</para></listitem>
